# Allowlist, not a denylist.
#
# ~/.claude is stowed from this directory, so Claude Code writes ALL of its
# runtime state in here — currently ~1.5 GB across plugins/, security/ and
# projects/. New state directories appear with every release, so enumerating
# what to EXCLUDE is a losing game. Instead: ignore everything, then re-include
# the handful of files that are actually configuration.
#
# NOTE: `.claude/*` (single star) is deliberate. Git cannot re-include a path
# whose PARENT directory is excluded, so `.claude/**` would make the `!` lines
# below silently inert. Excluding only the direct children keeps them workable.

# Machine-local Claude Code state, never versioned.
.claude.json
.claude.json.backup

# Ignore everything under .claude/ ...
.claude/*

# ... then re-include only real configuration.
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/statusline-command.sh
!.claude/skills/

# Local per-machine overrides stay out even though settings.json is in.
.claude/settings.local.json
